 Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
 
+## Logout
+
+A volunteer can call `logout(member_id)` in [the session module](../../larder/sessions.py) after a member reports a
+stolen phone. It revokes every session for that member before returning, so subsequent verification on any web
+server rejects those cookies. Other members stay logged in. A member can log in again after authenticating.
+Database failures propagate to the caller; a failed logout must not be reported as successful.
+
+Cookies issued before sessions had database records require a fresh login when this change is deployed.
+
 ## Shaped by
 
 - [Keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)
